    {
      "id": "claim_280409c69e694f8e93fff9c91b99d0af",
      "statement": "A chat turn begins with sendChatMessage: the message is prepared (slash command or prompt, attachments canonicalized per provider support), the chat's uncommitted change rows are materialized into a durable changes message, and the prompt commit happens in one synchronous storage transaction that also sets activeAgent — the lock behind assertChatNotActive's rejection of concurrent turns; built-in slash commands like /compact run a turn with no prompt.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-backend/src/overseer.ts#L5343-L5406",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6eeaf25b8885d19956734ea6b1aa29b46e618603b17ec405887dafc525370db9:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_29aa86adc8ce498ebe23b1590c341830",
      "statement": "Before a user-initiated agent turn, the overseer runs checkUsageAndBalance (a no-op allow when the Cloudflare limits flow is disabled): a block posts an agent error message with outcome usage_limit, and when the free tier is exhausted but the user has a funded Cloudflare account the resolved BYOK routing is reused so inference bills the user's account; callback-initiated continuations are exempt so outstanding callbacks are never stranded mid-flow.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-backend/src/overseer.ts#L5740-L5773",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ff399ac1357ee152521f5b6a77e3ad7b6d3fde57f0d16ea9c9e09d8fbd511ed1:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ec6e635ba70946b0957ff1b8d0202238",
      "statement": "The turn loop reruns runAgent after committing a compaction checkpoint (bounded, because the boundary only moves forward), ends after /compact, and for callback-initiated runs keeps looping while callbacks are outstanding — nudging once with the outstanding env.PARAMS_<n> names and then rejecting all remaining callbacks and ending with outcome callbacks_stalled if no progress followed the nudge; the Overseer's alarm holds the DO open and resumes agents when the browser closed.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-backend/src/overseer.ts#L5788-L5858",
