      "id": "claim_3053ec881ad041849b62eec337b3df67",
      "statement": "A transient RestoreForgerImpl capability passed as a run() argument grafts the runtime restore symbol onto each gadget's service binding in env, letting executed code forge persistent gadget stubs for hooks; the capability lives exactly as long as the execution and resolves binding names against the execution's own binding map, so it conveys no authority beyond the env it accompanies — and invalid stored binding names are skipped rather than crashing env construction.",
